        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Bayer 04 Leverkusen, Bayer Leverkusen\n- Places: BayArena, Leverkusen, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, Hochneukirch\n- People: Willibert Kremer, Robin Dutt, Jupp Heynckes\n- Roles: football coach, former player, scout, manager\n- Competitions: Bundesliga\n- Topics: German football league system\n\nFacts:\n- BayArena is a football stadium in Leverkusen, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, and it has been the home ground of Bundesliga club Bayer Leverkusen since 1958.\n- Willibert Kremer was born on 15 October 1939 in Hochneukirch.\n- Bayer 04 Leverkusen plays in the Bundesliga, the top tier of the German football league system, and hosts matches at the BayArena.\n- On 21 March 2011, Jupp Heynckes confirmed that he would not extend his stay at BayArena as manager of Bayer Leverkusen.\n- Starting with the 2011–12 season, Robin Dutt signed a two-year managerial contract with Bayer Leverkusen.\n- Willibert Kremer is a German football coach and former player who works as a scout with Bayer 04 Leverkusen.",
